  "theorem_statement": "The twenty-four registered ten-cycles form one orbit under the full 480-element automorphism group of native G60. Each cycle has setwise stabilizer order 20. The cycles are partitioned into twelve invariant two-cycle blocks, one for each quotient pentagon, and these blocks form one orbit with stabilizer order 40.",
  "interpretation": {
    "earned": "Registered pentagon closure is one homogeneous native geometry, not a collection of unrelated examples.",
    "pairing": "The two complete returns above one visible pentagon are intrinsically paired by the full symmetry."
  },
